Bug 2052807 - Do not re-add items of a hidden or removed calendar to the view when an in-flight read completes. r=darktrojan

`CalendarFilteredViewMixin` reads a calendar's items asynchronously in `#refreshCalendar` and checks the calendar's visibility only before the read starts. When the calendar is hidden or removed while the read is in flight, its items are cleaned from the view, but the read still completes afterwards and adds them back.

Enabling the offline support triggers this: `changeCalendarCache` removes the calendar and re-creates it under a new id. A refresh of the old calendar that is still in flight then re-adds its items, colorless because the calendar's style rules are gone, and nothing removes them again.

This is not specific to ICS calendars; any cached calendar (for example CalDAV) shows it, so the fix belongs in the shared view layer rather than in a provider.

Re-check the calendar's visibility after the read completes, before adding its items.

Add a browser test that subscribes an ICS calendar, enables its offline support and asserts that no item of the old calendar id lingers in the view.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310600


diff --git a/calendar/base/content/widgets/calendar-filter.js b/calendar/base/content/widgets/calendar-filter.js
--- a/calendar/base/content/widgets/calendar-filter.js
+++ b/calendar/base/content/widgets/calendar-filter.js
@@ -1312,17 +1312,20 @@ let CalendarFilteredViewMixin = Base =>
       const iterator = cal.iterate.streamValues(this.#filter.getItems(calendar));
       this.#iterators.add(iterator);
       const items = await Array.fromAsync(iterator);
       if (!this.#iterators.has(iterator)) {
         // #invalidate() cancelled this refresh while we were awaiting results.
         // Don't add stale items to the (now cleared) view of a newer refresh.
         return;
       }
-      this.addItems(items.flat());
+      // Skip if the calendar was hidden or removed while the read was in flight.
+      if (this.#isCalendarVisible(calendar)) {
+        this.addItems(items.flat());
+      }
       this.#iterators.delete(iterator);
     }
 
     /**
      * Implement this method to remove all items from the UI.
      */
     clearItems() {}
 
